  "summary": "Updates `feature_versionbits_warning.py` to wait for both invocations of the `-alertnotify` command instead of only the first. The test now waits for the pre-restart alert to write to the file, and truncates the alert log during node restart so the final check requires the second alert.",
  "problem": "The test previously verified the alert log only once at the end. Because the command appends to the file, the first alert satisfied the final check, allowing the test to exit while the second alert command was still launching. On Windows, this triggered intermittent cleanup failures (`PermissionError: [WinError 32]`) when attempting to delete the test directory while the child process held open inherited handles.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description quotes Windows failure: 'PermissionError: [WinError 32] The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process'",
    "PR description states it 'mitigates https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/28529'"
  ],
